Rule 1 (x and q must be floating tensors of the same dtype (float32 or float64))
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_2) ∧ min(v_1, v_1 / 2.0) = min(v_1, v_1 / 2.0) ∧ min(v_2, v_2 / 2.0) = min(v_2, v_2 / 2.0)
>>
Rule 2 (x and q must be broadcastable in shape)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= (ndim(v_1) = 0) ∨ (ndim(v_2) = 0) ∨ (ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : (shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)) ∨ (shape(v_1, i) = 1) ∨ (shape(v_2, i) = 1))
>>
Rule 3 (name is a benign non-placeholder string)
{v_3 : str} |= v_3 ≠ "none"
